  "Give it a name": "Bitte Namen eingeben",
  "A bit bigger, please — draw that one again.": "Etwas größer bitte — noch einmal zeichnen.",
  "Straight lines are taken as scrolling. Draw a shape with a turn in it.": "Gerade Linien gelten als Scrollen. Zeichne eine Form mit Richtungswechsel.",
  "Got it. Again.": "Passt. Noch einmal.",
  "Looks distinct from the other gestures. Save it.": "Unterscheidet sich klar von anderen Gesten. Speichern.",
  "Saved, but it can't be used with one finger: it isn't a closed shape": "Gespeichert, aber mit einem Finger nicht nutzbar: Form ist offen",
  "A cross is two quick diagonal strokes, which is exactly what two flicks look like while scrolling a feed or moving a map. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Ein Kreuz ähnelt zwei schnellen Wischern beim Scrollen und würde mit einem Finger zufällig auslösen.",
  "This is two straight lines with one corner. Ordinary drags, swipes between photos and the back gesture draw that shape all the time, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Zwei Linien mit einer Ecke ähneln normalen Zurück- oder Fotowischgesten zu sehr.",
  "Part of this digit is an open line, and a scroll that curls at the end can look just like it. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Teile dieser Ziffer sind offen und ähneln gebogenem Scrollen.",
  "A one-finger swipe is how every app scrolls.": "Ein-Finger-Wischen dient in jeder App zum Scrollen.",
  "This digit is an open line that doesn't end where it starts. A curved scroll or swipe in an app can draw the same shape, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Diese Ziffer endet nicht am Startpunkt und würde beim Scrollen auslösen.",
  "With one finger only closed shapes are allowed (one stroke that ends where it started), because ordinary scrolls and swipes never do that. This custom gesture isn't drawn that way.": "Mit einem Finger sind nur geschlossene Formen erlaubt (ein Zug bis zum Startpunkt).",
